      "id": "513c93ef-864e-4019-b2d5-d4bbaf063319",
      "name": "Format transcript fields",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1000,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Extract YouTube and TikTok transcripts to clean text\n\nPaste a mixed list of YouTube and TikTok links and get one clean row per video: title, author, word count and the full transcript. Use it as the first step for summaries, blog posts, newsletters or a RAG knowledge base.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Set video links** holds your list. YouTube videos, Shorts, playlists, whole channels (`https://www.youtube.com/@handle`) and TikTok links (including `tiktok.com/t/...` share links) can be mixed.\n2. **Split links by platform** groups the links so each platform is one batch request.\n3. **Get transcripts from Apify** calls two Apify Actors synchronously (no polling). YouTube videos without captions are transcribed with Whisper (`aiFallback: true`).\n4. **Format transcript fields** returns `status, url, title, author, source, wordCount, transcript`. Private, deleted or music-only videos come back as `no_transcript`.\n\n### Setup steps (2 min)\n1. Create an Apify account and copy your API token (Console > Settings > API & Integrations).\n2. Open **Get transcripts from Apify** and create a *Header Auth* credential: Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer <your token>`.\n3. Replace the example links in **Set video links** and click *Execute workflow*.\n\n### Customization\nConnect the last node to an AI model (summaries, hooks), Google Sheets (one row per video) or a vector store.\n\n*Disclosure: I maintain both Apify Actors used here.*",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 560
      },
      "name": "Template overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -640,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Add your links\nEdit the list in **Set video links**. YouTube and TikTok links can be mixed.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Step 1 note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
